# SLURM Deconvolution Batch Template

Dec 3, 2024 — Chris Anto (canto@uchicago.edu)
Jul 7, 2026 — NPMitchell (npmitchell@uchicago.edu)

This directory is a template for running multi-view deconvolution as a batch job on RCC. **Copy this directory elsewhere before editing** — don't modify the template in place — then follow the full protocol on [LabResources](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1POgY4802YNJ5gKTr1Buk5kvwCBillGMHnD1IpRqOSRE/edit?usp=sharing).

## How it fits together

`decon_main.sh` (sbatch job) → `deconvolve_timepoints.sh` → Fiji headless → `batch_macro.bsh` (ImageJ/Fiji macro)

- **`decon_main.sh`** — the `sbatch` script. Sets the partition, memory, cpus-per-task, and the timepoint range (as a job array).
- **`deconvolve_timepoints.sh`** — called by `decon_main.sh`; launches Fiji headless (via `xvfb-run`) and runs the macro.
- **`batch_macro.bsh`** — the ImageJ/Fiji macro that actually performs the deconvolution.

## Setup

1. Copy this directory elsewhere and `cd` into your copy.
2. Edit **`batch_macro.bsh`** for your dataset:
   - XML dataset directory
   - Processing channel
   - Timepoint(s)
   - Bounding box limits
   - Number of iterations
   - Output file directory
   - PSF paths (specified by mag and excitation)

   Leave everything else unchanged, or the macro won't work.
3. Edit **`decon_main.sh`** for cluster resources and timepoint selection (see below).

## Cluster (partition) settings

The only CPU/partition configurations that work on RCC's shared partitions:

| Partition | mem | cpus-per-task |
|---|---|---|
| `caslake` | `0G` | `40` |
| `amd`     | `0G` | `64` |

The `amd` config above is what we use for large bounding boxes (e.g. midgut at 33x). Also set `time` (walltime), `account=pi-npmitchell`, and a job name.

For other configurations, see the [RCC partitions guide](https://rcc-uchicago.github.io/user-guide/partitions/#configurations); the [RCC user guide](https://rcc-uchicago.github.io/user-guide/) has more general info and is worth reading.

Fiji is expected at `/project/npmitchell/fiji-linux64/Fiji.app/`. If you need a different installation, update the path in `deconvolve_timepoints.sh` (let Chris know if you think you need this).

## Running the job

From your copied directory on RCC:

```bash
sbatch decon_main.sh
```

Check job status:
```bash
squeue -u <cnetID>
```

Cancel a job:
```bash
scancel <jobID>
```
